# BullPen Coding Standards

## Tech Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4
- **Data**: Supabase (auth, Postgres), TanStack Query
- **UI**: Radix UI, Framer Motion, Lucide icons
- **Charts**: D3, Recharts
- **Validation**: Zod

## General Best Practices

- **Imports**: Use `@/` path alias for project imports (e.g. `@/components/ui/button`)
- **Client components**: Add `'use client'` at top of file when using hooks, browser APIs, or event handlers
- **Server by default**: Prefer server components; use client only when necessary
- **Type safety**: Avoid `any`; use proper types from `@/lib/types` or database types
- **Error handling**: Surface user-friendly messages; log details server-side

## React & Next.js

- Use functional components and hooks
- Colocate data fetching with components via `useQuery` or server components
- Use `<Suspense>` for async boundaries; provide meaningful fallbacks
- Prefer `router.replace()` over `window.location` for client-side navigation
- Metadata in layout/page for SEO

## File Conventions

- **Components**: `components/<domain>/<Name>.tsx` (PascalCase)
- **Hooks**: `hooks/use-<name>.ts` (kebab-case)
- **Lib/utils**: `lib/<domain>/<name>.ts`
- **API routes**: `app/api/<route>/route.ts`
- **Pages**: `app/<path>/page.tsx`

## Supabase & Auth

- Use `createBrowserClient()` for client; `createServerClient()` for server/API
- Auth state is event-driven via `onAuthStateChange`; avoid timing workarounds
- RLS policies protect data; never bypass with service role in client code
- Profile loading only after session exists

## Styling (Tailwind)

- Use Tailwind utility classes; avoid inline styles unless dynamic
- Prefer `cn()` or `clsx` for conditional classes
- Dark mode by default; use `text-foreground`, `bg-background`
- Keep responsive classes: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` where layout differs

## Data & API

- Validate inputs with Zod before DB operations
- Use TanStack Query for client caching; `staleTime` for infrequent data
- API routes: return `{ success, data?, error? }` consistently
- Handle loading and error states in UI

## Code Quality

- Prefer early returns over deep nesting
- Extract reusable logic into hooks or lib functions
- Keep components under ~200 lines; split when larger
- Use meaningful variable names; avoid abbreviations except `id`, `url`, `ctx`
